1. She is British and currently living in England. (Verbatim: "I'm back in England... I was still British while I was away... Because that's not curable.")  
2. She recently returned from a trip to Japan where she spent most of July. (Verbatim: "I have been in Japan for pretty much the whole of July and I've just come back.")  
3. She speaks Japanese and improved her language skills during her stay in Japan. (Verbatim: "In Japan, I got like nihongojozu'd every, every single, like, day.")  
4. She has a singing voice that she describes as soft, and she used to be in a choir. (Verbatim: "I sing. I do sing. I was a choir girl. My issue is my singing voice is a bit on the soft side.")  
5. She owns a fluffy dog who became ill while she was away in Japan. (Verbatim: "I got a fluffy dog... she got a bit ill, literally, like, after I left for Japan.")  
6. She brought Japanese dog treats, a new collar, and a Japan-shaped squeaky toy back for her dog from Japan. (Verbatim: "I got her dog treats from Japan. I got her a new collar from Japan... the shape of Japan, the island shape. And it says Japan and it squeaks.")  
7. She experienced a nightmare about being forgotten by her audience after returning. (Verbatim: "I had a dream that I screamed and nobody turned up... 'What do you mean welcome back? Who the heck are you?'")  
8. She forgot to bring the dongle for her headset while in Japan, rendering her headphones unusable. (Verbatim: "One of the things I forgot to bring... was, I have my little headset with me, I forgot the little dongle to go with it.")  
9. She enjoys crane games and brought back many items from Japan, including figurines. (Verbatim: "I got the joy of crane games a bit too much... a lot of figurines to show you.")  
10. She plans to record music and has been preparing for a cover, though she hasn’t finalized the song. (Verbatim: "I've been meaning to swap out my audio box thingy for a while... I literally have everything ready for this cover, except for the... the song.") [end of text]



1. Her full name is Elia Stellaria. (Verbatim: "hi hello ladies I'm Elias Delaria" – note: likely a mispronunciation or typo of "Elia Stellaria".)
2. She is British. (Verbatim: "I'd say england and they were always very quite shocked.")
3. She recently returned from an almost month-long trip to Japan. (Verbatim: "I've just come back from my almost month-long trip to Japan.")
4. She is sensitive to loud noises and experiences motion sickness on public transport. (Verbatim: "I'd be sat on the train like with my eyes closed because you know motion sickness i'd be like ow i can hear tourists being really loud no stop stop stop it hurts me.")
5. She finds queue-cutting deeply upsetting. (Verbatim: "what was upsetting was when when people cut the queue that is truly upsetting.")
6. She appreciates orderly queues and has a cultural affinity for them as a British person. (Verbatim: "i'm british so i don't mind queues i quite like the order.")
7. She has difficulty understanding when people speak to her in Japanese. (Verbatim: "I didn't think anyone would speak to me... I just didn't register them.")
8. She values Japanese customer service for being polite and kind, in contrast to her experience with British service. (Verbatim: "in japan it's very very polite like all the customer service that i experienced there was very very kind very happy.")
9. She made an effort to learn about Japanese etiquette before her trip. (Verbatim: "i did do my best to to look up as much as possible regarding japanese etiquette because there is a lot that is different compared to british etiquette.")
10. She has a fear of being approached or flirted with unexpectedly. (Verbatim: "Lily was like Elliot they're trying to flirt with you I was like who... I ran away like like a smart person would.") [end of text]



1. She recently took an unusually long break from streaming, longer than her typical one or two days. (Verbatim: "i've never had a break this long like even one or two days is a bit too low on chatium for me")  
2. She is trying to take better care of herself, motivated by her community and the idea that her fans will also take care of themselves. (Verbatim: "i'm trying to look after myself um so i hope that even while i've been away you've all been looking after yourselves right")  
3. She plans to return to a regular streaming schedule, with updates expected on Sundays. (Verbatim: "i'll be back to streaming regularly so i can keep reminding you all to look after yourselves um keep an eye out for a schedule to be posted on um sunday")  
4. She feels deep gratitude toward her community for welcoming her back kindly and not forgetting her. (Verbatim: "the fact that you all decided to welcome me back so kindly i i appreciate it but appreciate doesn't even feel like a strong enough word")  
5. She refers to her mother as "mama elia" and mentions that her mother is going to or has visited "asia land." (Verbatim: "mama elia having to is actually going to asia land um so i literally just came back from asia land")  
6. She intended to have a short stream (1–1.5 hours) but ended up streaming for three hours. (Verbatim: "this was supposed to be like a short stream like like short short like one hour or one hour and a half not three hours")  
7. She experienced lightheadedness during the stream, which she suspects may be from a can of jet (possibly a drink or aerosol). (Verbatim: "i'm assuming the lightheadedness is from is from this can jet like give you lightheadedness")  
8. She missed doing member-only streams and looks forward to having cozy, intimate interactions with her community again. (Verbatim: "we'll also have to do a member stream i've missed member streams with you all i've missed that a lot our cozy cozy times")  
9. She describes her streaming style as letting her internal stream of thoughts come directly out of her mouth. (Verbatim: "the way that this works is i i just sort of let the thoughts that are in my brain come straight out of my mouth")  
10. She likes the scent of mangoes and humorously expresses a desire to smell like them. (Verbatim: "i want to smell like mangoes yeah um okay i'll go get the sleeves") [end of text]



1. Her primary goal as a VTuber is to make people happy and reach as many people as possible. (Verbatim: "my goal my super super super super super goal is to make people happy... to make people happy i want to try and reach as many people as possible")

2. She is originally from England and identifies with British culture, including a British accent. (Verbatim: "Did Japan change my accent? Did it? Oh no. Did I lose? Did I lose some Britishness?")

3. She recently returned from a trip to Japan, where she visited the Nintendo Store and the Pokemon Center. (Verbatim: "Yeah, I went to the Nintendo store. And I went to the Pokemon Center.")

4. She drinks English breakfast tea daily and maintained this habit while in Japan. (Verbatim: "I did have a cup of tea in the morning. So I kept to that.")

5. She brought back various Japanese teas, including Pokemon-themed tea, as souvenirs. (Verbatim: "I did bring back some other kinds of tea. I will show you pictures of those. I got myself some Pokemon tea.")

6. She enjoys food with cute packaging, particularly biscuits, and bought many for their appearance. (Verbatim: "they come in the cute packaging so i am a sucker for that so i bought it")

7. She wants to improve her Japanese language skills after struggling to communicate during her trip. (Verbatim: "one thing i do want to do... is definitely improve my japanese i felt bad because like first getting nihongo joe's dude hurts")

8. She had an awkward experience at a maid cafe bar in Japan where the staff didn’t speak English. (Verbatim: "accidentally going to that his desk maid cafe bar that was awkward... those maids didn't speak the tiniest bit of english at all")

9. She had a difficult and lonely childhood in England, especially during summer holidays, due to being sheltered and lacking friends. (Verbatim: "remember july for me it was really a sort of like a meh kind of month... being a very sheltered child that didn't have friends um i didn't go out so it was a difficult month")

10. She does not get angry or rage while playing games, even when they are frustrating. (Verbatim: "i'm never ever ever ever ever ever ever rage to the game") [end of text]



1. She has a diagnosed agoraphobia, which involves fear of uncontrolled spaces and crowds. (Verbatim: "i have agoraphobia um so i have like an official diagnosis from a doctor... it's more of like a fear of being in a uncontrolled um space like an uncontrolled space is sort of like along with but then it's also those spaces are spaces with people")

2. She was a shut-in for a period before getting professional help to manage her agoraphobia. (Verbatim: "i was a shut in for a while for a while i was a shut in i was a shut it like a official shut in um so i yeah got help so that i wouldn't be such a shut in")

3. The global lockdown during the pandemic reversed her progress with agoraphobia, which she found deeply ironic and frustrating. (Verbatim: "then i was like yeah i'm so good at being out it's like... and then obviously lockdown ended i've been like adjusting back")

4. She gets travel sickness, especially in trains, and cannot read or look at her phone while traveling. (Verbatim: "i get travel sick so i normally look out the window... i can't really read i'll feel sick because i'll travel sick")

5. She finds comfort in orderly environments and appreciates Japan’s structured crowd movement, which helped reduce her anxiety. (Verbatim: "in japan it's like natural for people to have some kind of order with their crowds... that removed a lot of stress that i would normally have with crowds")

6. She dislikes seagulls and finds them aggressive, especially in England where they steal food. (Verbatim: "seagulls are scary... they will steal your food while you eat it... they will okay like even if you're holding your food and you've got your eye on it")

7. She prefers crows and sparrows over seagulls, based on her observations during a trip to Japan. (Verbatim: "i prefer crows and sparrows to to seagulls... i encountered a lot of um crows there were a lot of crows in japan but i didn't experience any seagulls")

8. She feels guilty about walking and eating in public, particularly when she ate an ice cream cone while walking in Japan. (Verbatim: "i just felt so bad i was like walking along and i was like do it looking around like it's suspicious... i've never felt so guilty licking ice cream ever")

9. She once attempted to sing and has plans for a future karaoke stream. (Verbatim: "my attempts to sing i know i owe you a karaoke stream i do owe you all a karaoke stream")

10. She considered doing an ASMR stream but is unsure what it would involve. (Verbatim: "perhaps one day an asmr stream maybe maybe i i don't know i still don't know what the heck one would do") [end of text]



1. She climbed Mount Fuji during a trip and reached the summit despite severe weather conditions. (Verbatim: "I climbed Mount Fuji during my trip... I did it I did it I got a stick to show you as well to prove it")

2. She attempted to climb Mount Fuji at night to see the sunrise but encountered a storm with 60-70 km/h winds, rain, and freezing temperatures. (Verbatim: "I left the hut at like midnight... it was freezing and I was like yo what happened")

3. She ignored a warning from a guide at the final station advising climbers to wait due to dangerous weather. (Verbatim: "The guy stopped me... we advise you wait until past sunrise... I was like okay I'm gonna do it")

4. She has a fear of vomiting in public, especially during intense physical experiences. (Verbatim: "My only thought during that entire ride... don't you dare throw up Elliot don't throw up")

5. She once rode an attraction that caused motion sickness, leading her to close her eyes, scream, and cry throughout. (Verbatim: "I closed my eyes for the entire ride while screaming and and crying")

6. She considers herself expressive and is currently using a temporary VTuber model. (Verbatim: "You got more expressions to come because this is a temp remodel")

7. Her debut as a VTuber is upcoming and will happen as soon as her permanent model is ready. (Verbatim: "The next exciting event... coming soon... it will be my debut")

8. She plans to create comedy skit shorts featuring herself and a character named Eleanor after debut. (Verbatim: "I'd like to do shorts where it's more like little comedy skit kind of things which should be like between me and Eleanor")

9. She is unable to record content ideas until her permanent model is ready, which she finds frustrating. (Verbatim: "It's really frustrating to not be able to record any of that... I just have my list of ideas that just sit there")

10. She values kindness and self-care, emphasizing that viewers should take care of themselves over watching her stream. (Verbatim: "Rule number zero is be kind and rule number one is take care of yourself okay that's the priority here") [end of text]



1. She used to enjoy singing and making up songs as a child but was frequently told to be quiet by family members. (Verbatim: "i actually used to like singing a lot as a kid... i just remember always getting told off by papa ellia mama ellia ellie bros being like shut up")  
