1. She recently returned from a trip to Japan, which left her extremely tired and feeling ill upon return. (Verbatim: "i felt all like shiverish and yeah i wasn't maybe i'm just maybe this is just like exhaustion because i'll be honest oh gosh like japan it was very as amazing and wonderful as the place it is i was very very very very very very very very tired")

2. She visited multiple locations in Japan, including Tokyo, Osaka, Kyoto, Kinosaki, and the area around Mount Fuji with Lake Kawaguchi. (Verbatim: "so i went to um tokyo of course i went to tokyo i went to osaka i went to kyoto and i went to this lovely like more rural place known for its onsen called kinosaki")

3. She climbed Mount Fuji despite bad weather, choosing not to reschedule her hut reservation. (Verbatim: "but sometimes if you want to climb when the weather's bad you can like change it but i still climbed it anyway because i thought i don't want to rearrange my hut")

4. She finds large crowds and people recording in public spaces stressful, especially in places like Shibuya Crossing and the bamboo forest. (Verbatim: "one thing i did struggle with um was that like there's even though the crowds are like organized it is still a lot of people like going outside and seeing so many people you know so many and i've never seen so many people with heckin cameras and recording")

