10. She has difficulty winning crane games for plushies or figures she really wants, but succeeds more easily with smaller or edible prizes. (Verbatim: "apparently if it's like small or edible i'm okay but if it's like a figurine or a plushie that i really want it's a no") [end of text]



1. She collects figurines of characters she likes, particularly from the game Umamusume. (Verbatim: "ones of characters i like or crane games turns out i've got a lot of umamusami characters now")

2. She owns at least three Megamin figurines and resists buying more despite strong temptation. (Verbatim: "i had to hold myself back on i wanted to buy megamin figurines because i have three")

3. She has a collection of anime-themed mugs and glasses, including Corner Silver and Yorekamp merchandise. (Verbatim: "i bought a corner silver mug and the corner silver glass and i also bought a lot of yorekamp stuff and some jujitsu kaisen")

4. She owns a high-quality, expensive Japanese kitchen knife which she intends to care for properly. (Verbatim: "i got a fancy japanese knife... i'm gonna look after this i'm gonna look after this so that knife is gonna get taken care of nicely because it was expensive")

5. She previously owned poorly maintained knives that were kept in a drawer and washed in the dishwasher. (Verbatim: "they're in pretty terrible condition... they're in awful condition which is why i'd rather just use the scissors")

6. She tried high-quality wagyu beef in Japan and found it exceptionally delicious. (Verbatim: "i did try wagyu like the nicest wagyu i could find um it was so nice so yummy it was so it was it was like nothing i'd eaten before")

7. She has difficulty reading Japanese and relies on Google Translate, which sometimes fails to provide accurate translations. (Verbatim: "i tried to use google translate on these little labels but it didn't work... it came up with the most random words")

8. She visited Kinosaki and stayed in a traditional Japanese inn (ryokan), where she ate unfamiliar traditional food without knowing what it was. (Verbatim: "when i went to kinosaki i stayed in a ryokun so like a traditional a traditional inn and i got to have um traditional japanese")

9. She prefers Coca-Cola over alcoholic drinks and avoids drinking to prevent hangovers during travel. (Verbatim: "i really like coca-cola... i felt like if i drank i'd be hung over the next day and then i'd be sad")

10. She does not take photos of food habitually, often eating first when hungry, especially with non-anime themed meals. (Verbatim: "i'm not in the habit of taking photos so i'll like eat it and be like wait a second") [end of text]



